Based on the specifications of the 7420 chip, which contains two independent 4-input NAND gates, we need to implement the logic function $Y = \overline{A \cdot B \cdot C \cdot D}$ for both output channels.

Here is the Verilog implementation for the `TopModule`:

```verilog
module TopModule (
  input p1a,
  input p1b,
  input p1c,
  input p1d,
  output p1y,
  input p2a,
  input p2b,
  input p2c,
  input p2d,
  output p2y
);

  // First 4-input NAND gate
  // p1y is low only if all inputs (p1a, p1b, p1c, p1d) are high
  assign p1y = ~(p1a & p1b & p1c & p1d);

  // Second 4-input NAND gate
  // p2y is low only if all inputs (p2a, p2b, p2c, p2d) are high
  assign p2y = ~(p2a & p2b & p2c & p2d);

endmodule
